    "text": "There are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> students in class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If the number of ways, in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> students can be selected from them so as to include at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> students from each class and at most <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> students from the total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> students of class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
